  "claim": "Royler Gracie was a student of the person who also taught Romero Cavalcanti and ran the Gracie Humaitá school in Botafogo.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Rolls Gracie. Sentence: Rolls Gracie ([ˈɡɾejsi] 1951–1982) was a Brazilian martial artist.\nPage: Rolls Gracie. Sentence: He was teacher of Rickson Gracie, Carlos Gracie Jr., Royler Gracie, Márcio \"Macarrão\" Stambowsky, Rigan Machado and Romero \"Jacare\" Cavalcanti.\nPage: Royler Gracie. Sentence: He ran the Gracie Humaitá school in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil for many years under his father Helio's direction, but currently lives in San Diego.\nPage: Rodrigo Medeiros. Sentence: He received his black belt from Rolls Gracie student, Romero \"Jacaré\" Cavalcanti, he also trained under Fernando 'Magrao' Gurgel and is one of a select group of Jiu-Jitsu competitors to have won the prestigious World Jiu-Jitsu Championship openweight titles twice.",
