      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "245a1dc0-79f8-5314-be19-537bd3a4ce98",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rolls Gracie, Rickson Gracie, Carlos Gracie Jr., Royler Gracie, Márcio \"Macarrão\" Stambowsky, Rigan Machado, Romero \"Jacare\" Cavalcanti, Rodrigo Medeiros, Hélio Gracie, Fernando \"Magrao\" Gurgel\n- Places: Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, San Diego\n- Organizations: Gracie Humaitá school\n- Roles: Brazilian martial artist, teacher, student\n- Events: World Jiu-Jitsu Championship\n\nFacts:\n- Rolls Gracie was a Brazilian martial artist who lived from 1951 to 1982.\n- Rolls Gracie taught Rickson Gracie, Carlos Gracie Jr., Royler Gracie, Márcio \"Macarrão\" Stambowsky, Rigan Machado, and Romero \"Jacare\" Cavalcanti.\n- Royler Gracie ran the Gracie Humaitá school in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil for many years under his father Hélio Gracie's direction.\n- Royler Gracie currently lives in San Diego.\n- Rodrigo Medeiros received his black belt from Romero \"Jacaré\" Cavalcanti, who was a student of Rolls Gracie.\n- Rodrigo Medeiros also trained under Fernando \"Magrao\" Gurgel.\n- Rodrigo Medeiros is one of a select group of Jiu-Jitsu competitors to have won the World Jiu-Jitsu Championship openweight title twice.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d8b1a8aa-9e6b-50db-a571-b32e0813c647",
        "text": "Page: Rolls Gracie. Sentence: Rolls Gracie ([ˈɡɾejsi] 1951–1982) was a Brazilian martial artist.\nPage: Rolls Gracie. Sentence: He was teacher of Rickson Gracie, Carlos Gracie Jr., Royler Gracie, Márcio \"Macarrão\" Stambowsky, Rigan Machado and Romero \"Jacare\" Cavalcanti.\nPage: Royler Gracie. Sentence: He ran the Gracie Humaitá school in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil for many years under his father Helio's direction, but currently lives in San Diego.\nPage: Rodrigo Medeiros. Sentence: He received his black belt from Rolls Gracie student, Romero \"Jacaré\" Cavalcanti, he also trained under Fernando 'Magrao' Gurgel and is one of a select group of Jiu-Jitsu competitors to have won the prestigious World Jiu-Jitsu Championship openweight titles twice.",
